    "evidence": "docs/COPPEROS_BOOT_PROOF_2026-10-16.json",
    "selectionNote": "Selected from docs/COPPERSTART_APP.md and CopperScreen/Firmware/CopperStart.json at task start. Concurrent later consumer qualification edits are excluded; these replays always use the recorded dev.3 ROM hash. This is engine/native-media evidence, not qualification of a later installed app or firmware pair."
  },
  "cause": "ComparisonSatisfied added the nominal horizontal-counter offset without wrapping at the line length. Physical PAL H225 became HP=$E4 instead of HP=$01. A late WAIT could therefore wake after missing its valid horizontal match, including the line-255 pointer reload seen in Superfrog.",
  "fix": "Wrap HP using the current line length before the existing WAIT/SKIP mask and comparison. Preserve bus grants, pending outputs, vertical comparison, guest code, media and viewport geometry.",
  "references": [
    {
      "title": "Commodore Amiga Hardware Reference Manual, chapter 2: WAIT and beam position",
      "url": "https://bastya.net/AmigaDevDocs/hard_2.html",
      "use": "The comparison uses the beam counters; normal PAL HP ends at $E2. The nominal-to-physical phase mapping is the engine's existing Copper input contract; independent physical collision timing is not newly certified."
    }
  ],
  "nativeTrace": {
    "path": "trace.log",
    "sha256": "08bcbb04d67300fd64d2e861f84fccf8e1650acfc106bdf09b8f89d291ae09eb",
